# acetylacetone.msf
# Acetylacetone (2,4-pentanedione)
# pKa=8.900 (C-H acid, beta-diketone: CH2 flanked by two C=O)
# Source: Perrin 1981
# Second C-H acid in training set after barbituric acid, but acyclic.
# The anion is a symmetric enolate — charge delocalised across O-C=C-C-O.
# Δq_O and Δq_C will be large; Δq_N=0. Unique among all training data.
# Important metal-chelating scaffold (Fe, Cu, Al coordination chemistry).

